The malicious links on jdownloader.org were live from about 00:01 UTC on 2026-05-06 until the server was shut down on 2026-05-07, not for about 48 hours, and only the Windows "Download Alternative Installer" links and the Linux shell installer link were affected. The vendor published hashes of the malicious substitutes, not a manifest of genuine files, and the check it gives is the AppWork GmbH signature; an independent analyst identified the Windows payload as a loader for a Python-based RAT, while the Linux installer plants a SUID-root binary and a login-script persistence.
